            <h3 class="fw-0 pt-3">Q: How does S. Phaneuf & Associates protect agricultural topsoil during site excavation in Stow, MA?</h3>
            <p>S. Phaneuf & Associates strips and stockpiles organic topsoil separately during initial earthmoving using bulldozers and excavators. Subgrade soil is excavated and graded for foundation footings or driveway aggregate bases. Stockpiled topsoil is subsequently re-spread over designated landscape zones to preserve Stow's fertile agricultural soil quality.</p>

            <h3 class="fw-0 pt-3">Q: Why is subgrade compaction critical for asphalt driveways in Stow, MA?</h3>
            <p>S. Phaneuf & Associates compacts driveway subgrade soils using 3-to-5 ton vibratory rollers to achieve maximum dry density. Proper compaction eliminates air voids in the underlying gravel, preventing heavy delivery trucks or agricultural equipment from causing wheel rutting and surface depression in the final asphalt pavement in Stow.</p>
